+# Newton tolerance per hit. The section-gap map is noisy: integration error is amplified by
+# the manifold's instability, so ||R|| cannot be driven below the map's own noise. For the
+# tertiary hit that noise was measured (#1075, docs/notes/2026-10-12-1075-os-update-numerics-
+# drift.md sec. 6.3; scripts/probe_1075_connection_hits.py tertiary_floor): 13-point line fits
+# through the phases at steps 1e-11..1e-9 leave a fit-residual std of up to sigma = 6.9e-8 (x,
+# along tau_s). The tolerance is k * sigma with k = 3 fixed before the re-run: 2e-7. Under the
+# old 1e-9 the tertiary hit converged only by luck and stopped converging after the macOS 27.0.1
+# update (Newton stalls at 3.4e-9, 4e-9 from the stored crossing). The other three hits keep
+# 1e-9 (not measured; they pass). Identity, ghost margin, Radau and re-approach bounds are
+# unchanged for every hit.
+_DEFAULT_NEWTON_TOL = 1e-9
+_TERTIARY_NEWTON_TOL = 2e-7
+
+
+def _newton_tol(hit: dict[str, int]) -> float:
+    return _TERTIARY_NEWTON_TOL if hit is _TERTIARY else _DEFAULT_NEWTON_TOL
+
 
